sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: the run of one command of proof:run on a proof task VM of its own (Nick + orchestrator, 2026-11-05). The Gateway admits the intent of the run; Orbit's own Swamp runs the provision, the cases and the destruction of the VM as children of the workflow operation-proof-run; the Gateway projects the run once. The cases are the workflow proof-fleet-verify and its batch and case children.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · started by proof:run
  %% kind: proof.command
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Proof task VM<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit the run<br/>group · VM · inputs
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - proof:run selected this command and its cases file, and made a task group for it
  %%> What it records:
  %%> - the task provision, the cases file, the pinned SSH target of the VM and the destruction of the VM, all as inputs; no step calls back
  GW->>SW: Start the parent run<br/>operation-proof-run
  SW->>VM: Provision the task VM<br/>child · operation-task-provision
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same provision every task uses; stage 2 of the chart of proof:run is part of it
  SW->>VM: Pin the host key<br/>of the new VM
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - fills the host key that the provision observed into the SSH target of the cases
  SW->>VM: Run the proof<br/>child · proof-fleet-verify
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the cases file of the command, the checkout path, the group and the pinned SSH target of the VM
  %%> - no secret
  SW->>VM: Select the cases<br/>runner plan --lines
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one line a batch, `BATCH SETUP CASE...`, in the order of `swamp/proof/batches.yaml`; inside a batch, in file order
  VM-->>SW: Ordered plan<br/>batches · cases
  loop each batch, one at a time
    Note over SW: Restore base<br/>built, not passed live
    %%> Built, not yet passed live:
    %%> - the restore of `base` before each batch is the workflow `proof-fleet-restore`, a step of the batch workflow; 0 of 2 runs succeeded by 2026-11-06; the old restore was removed
    opt the batch declares a start state
      SW->>VM: Set up the batch<br/>runner setup
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - runs the setup steps of the batch; a setup that fails or is not built stops the run
    end
    loop each case, one at a time, one child workflow
      SW->>VM: Run one case<br/>runner case ID
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - the step allows failure, so a failed case does not stop its batch
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - one JSON line of at most 1 KB: the case id, the verdict, the cause, the seconds and the failed checks
      opt the case did not pass and is not the last of its batch
        SW->>VM: Set up the batch again<br/>runner setup
        %%> Why:
        %%> - a failed case can leave anything behind; the setup of the batch runs again
        %%> - the last case of a batch skips it
        %%> Built, not yet passed live:
        %%> - the restore of `base` before the setup is the workflow `proof-fleet-restore` (0 of 2 runs succeeded by 2026-11-06); the old restore was removed
      end
    end
    Note over SW: Join the batch lines<br/>report
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - a case that printed no line is `failed` with cause `infrastructure`; a case that did not run is `unrun` with cause `infrastructure`
  end
  SW->>VM: Destroy the task VM<br/>child · always
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs after success and after failure, so no VM is left behind
  %%> - with `keep_failed` (see the chart of `proof:run`) a failed run skips it and the Gateway cancels the group 60 minutes later
  Note over SW: Join the verdicts<br/>Report step
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - every case of the plan has one line, in plan order; the Gateway reads this step once, when the run ends
  SW-->>GW: Native terminal result<br/>verdict lines
  Note over GW: Record the run once<br/>one row for each case
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Gateway records the VM, the verdicts and the end of the group, then closes the proof of the CLI when this was its last run
